    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Belmont was originally called Garibaldi Station and was renamed in 1886.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicbelmont.com/history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The railroad arrived in 1872, installing a water tank and fueling station at Garibaldi Station, the site that would become Belmont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicbelmont.com/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1876 the Caldwell Plantation was donated to Benedictine monks, leading to the founding of Belmont Abbey and shaping downtown Belmont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicbelmont.com/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "What began as a quiet settlement along the Catawba River has grown into a thriving town where history and progress meet at every turn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicbelmont.com/history/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first trolley line in East Portland, established in 1888, ran through Belmont and was later converted to a bus line in 1949.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belmont%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Early roots of Belmont include a fort built in the 1750s at the confluence of the Catawba and South Fork Rivers.",
